{"id": "EUVD-2026-76535", "enisaUuid": "203ab920-be39-3192-9b15-9cc2018558cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: mcp2221: stop device IO before hid_hw_stop\n\nQuiesce device IO at the start of the devm cleanup callback\nmcp2221_hid_unregister() so that incoming HID reports cannot race with\nhardware teardown during probe failure or device removal, addressing a\npotential use-after-free.\n\nGuard the call to hid_device_io_stop() with io_started. On normal\nremoval hid_device_remove() has already cleared io_started before the\ndevres group is released, so an unconditional call would otherwise hit\nthe !io_started path and emit a spurious \"io already stopped\" warning\non every removal. The guard preserves the probe-failure balancing,\nwhere io_started is still set after hid_device_io_start(), while\nstaying silent on the normal removal path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85d963499f1feeea287c0a37c3eac3fc1898eca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ae90a19e6b5a8557d25d95facb7e01c9c07af38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c99ba6c234d4d537c317336376b78c088174034a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2eda1513f573945c1e3a0090341f3d28740463b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dca151633c0fde90935311c60e7cfc064aa56134"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p59v-m859-4ppq", "CVE-2026-89623"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c36bd0c-914d-3bba-abea-fed0ffbcc109", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4b50ac06ea6e47bdd2b04e97d1090c673c80645 <0ae90a19e6b5a8557d25d95facb7e01c9c07af38"}, {"id": "5da81196-617a-346c-b051-b59f5b312748", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4b50ac06ea6e47bdd2b04e97d1090c673c80645 <2eda1513f573945c1e3a0090341f3d28740463b1"}, {"id": "7e52598e-48ba-3617-85f4-00557c79ab2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.8 <7.2.4"}, {"id": "8993b13e-2c5a-3121-b190-8d77341c1858", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.8 <6.12.109"}, {"id": "a63b6c61-abe5-3957-adb5-1396ad461192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4b50ac06ea6e47bdd2b04e97d1090c673c80645 <c99ba6c234d4d537c317336376b78c088174034a"}, {"id": "a98dc9b6-d5c1-3c22-a848-1eb5160690dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4b50ac06ea6e47bdd2b04e97d1090c673c80645 <dca151633c0fde90935311c60e7cfc064aa56134"}, {"id": "b69a3d6e-f887-3c4d-b17d-89493ac029b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.8 <6.18.50"}, {"id": "b8ba923e-797e-3f68-98f2-0fa5661802e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4b50ac06ea6e47bdd2b04e97d1090c673c80645 <85d963499f1feeea287c0a37c3eac3fc1898eca9"}, {"id": "e842cfc4-4f0e-3d96-8101-b5ff68e97fed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.8 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "e9eed612-af5c-33d6-89a8-625ceea52f4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.8 <7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "accb1810-5c8b-30ce-a86f-49a5463dd793", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}